<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Cookie Policy for FC Mobile Tools by TanzimFC.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / COOKIES</p>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: September 19, 2026</p>

    <section><h2>1. What cookies are</h2><p>Cookies are small pieces of information stored in a browser by a website or third-party service. Similar technologies can include local storage and other browser-side mechanisms.</p></section>

    <section><h2>2. Analytics cookies and similar technologies</h2><p>FCMOBILETOOLS uses Google Analytics on public pages. Google Analytics can use cookies and similar technologies to measure traffic, page usage, technical information, and aggregate site activity. Analytics is used to understand how the site is used and to improve its content and tools.</p></section>

    <section><h2>3. Authentication cookies</h2><p>The private admin and creator workspaces use HTTP-only, secure session cookies to keep authorized users signed in. These cookies are operational/security cookies for restricted areas rather than public advertising cookies. They have limited lifetimes and are cleared when the relevant session is logged out or expires.</p></section>

    <section><h2>4. Local storage</h2><p>Some tools and legacy features store progress, predictions, settings, balances, quiz state, or similar information in your browser's local storage. This is designed to keep tool state on your device. Clearing site data can remove that progress.</p></section>

    <section><h2>5. Third-party resources</h2><p>Public pages may load resources from third parties such as Google services and Cloudinary. External websites you open from links, including YouTube, Discord, X, EA services, and others, may set their own cookies or use similar technologies under their own policies.</p></section>

    <section><h2>6. Managing cookies and storage</h2><p>You can block, delete, or manage cookies and local storage through your browser settings. Some private authentication and site functionality may stop working correctly if required cookies or browser storage are blocked or cleared.</p></section>

    <section><h2>7. Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy when our analytics, authentication, tools, hosting, or third-party integrations change. The date above identifies the current version.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
